  "question": {
    "text": "If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Im</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></math>,&nbsp;(where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></math>) represents part of a circle, then the radius (in units) of the circle is (here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Im</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">z</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;represents the imaginary part of the complex number&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi><mo>)</mo></math>",
    "image": null
  },
